    "blocks": [
      {
        "id": "p1",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "The "
          },
          {
            "t": "em",
            "v": "caique"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " is an important part of Greek culture. For centuries, these traditional wooden boats have been used for fishing and for "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "transporting",
            "ref": "v-transport"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " goods, animals, and people. But the art of building caiques completely by hand is now in danger."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p2",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Caiques from the Greek island of Samos are famous for their quality. Years ago, quite a few boatbuilding centres could be found on the island, and many locals made a living building caiques. Now, only four boat builders remain. Giorgos Kiassos is one of them. “Sadly, I see the craft slowly dying,” he said while working on a boat. “Fewer and fewer people are ordering wooden boats. Boats made from materials like plastic are cheaper and sell better.”"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p3",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Few young locals are interested in taking up the craft. While the caique building is considered art, the work is tiring. It usually takes 5 to 6 years of hard training to learn to build a caique "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "independently",
            "ref": "v-independently"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". Kiassos tried to get his 26-year-old son to learn the craft, but the young man hopes to be a boat captain instead."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p4",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "The good news is that help is on the way. Kostas Damianidis is a researcher in traditional Greek boatbuilding. He is setting up a new craft museum on Samos. He also hopes to open a traditional boatbuilding school—the first in Greece—within the museum."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p5",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "To achieve his goals, Damianidis is turning to Kiassos for help. “It’s important to have someone with plenty of experience,” he said. After more than 30 years in the business, Kiassos knows when to cut down a tree and where each piece should go on the boat. With one mistake, the boat could have problems. When you get it all right, it combines beauty and "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "strength",
            "ref": "v-strength"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p6",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Kiassos is now finishing two caiques. “When a boat leaves, I’m sad,” he said. “Yes, I’m happy when everything’s okay. But it’s like something is leaving, like a piece of me.”"
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
